-- Default (26.7+): an unquoted integer for DateTime64 is a Unix timestamp in seconds
2023-12-23 20:37:33.000
2023-12-23 20:37:33.000
-- Setting compatibility to 26.6 restores the pre-26.7 raw scaled value (ticks)
1970-01-20 17:09:23.853
1970-01-20 17:09:23.853
-- The explicit input setting has the same effect as the compatibility rollback
1970-01-20 17:09:23.853
1970-01-20 17:09:23.853
-- DateTime: an unquoted integer is a whole number of seconds either way
2023-12-23 20:37:33
2023-12-23 20:37:33
-- DateTime: a fractional number is truncated by default, but rejected in compatibility mode
2023-12-23 20:37:33
-- JSONExtract: an unquoted integer for DateTime64 is seconds, consistent with a float
2023-12-23 20:37:33.000
2023-12-23 20:37:33.035
-- JSONExtract compatibility: an integer is the raw scaled value (ticks), a float stays seconds
1970-01-20 17:09:23.853
2023-12-23 20:37:33.035
-- JSONExtract: DateTime accepts a fractional number, truncated to whole seconds
2023-12-23 20:37:33
2023-12-23 20:37:33
-- JSONExtract compatibility: a fractional DateTime number is rejected (returns the default)
1970-01-01 00:00:00
2023-12-23 20:37:33
